# Inspect Kafka/JDK artifacts as data before compilation

This handoff gives the maintainer a bounded way to inspect the five
proposed test classpath JARs and their embedded version/legal text. It does not
approve them for execution. Root has now run ten unit tests and the bounded
offline JAR data inspection successfully. No compiler or acquired Java code has
run. The current findings, attribution gap and next execution gates are in
`kafka-artifact-verdict.md`. The original acquisition remains `complete:false`; the
separate legal-alias supplement resolves references only.

The actual fifth acquisition retained these final regular artifacts, with exact
paths, sizes and hashes in the original inventory. `jars.py` pins all five hashes.
The version labels below now agree with the actual embedded manifests/properties
as detailed in that verdict; source-to-binary equivalence remains unproven.

