## Actual retained image text and source relationships

Read-only inspection of the retained regular text established these facts:

- Kafka `opt/kafka/LICENSE` (`kafka-6-2409.data`, SHA
  `aaa8c150285f6e9921b2115858cd9631b52c31a18f4376750b80c6f80d605da7`)
  starts with Apache License2.0 and then inventories distribution components.
  Its list places lz4-java1.11.2 and snappy-java1.1.10.7 in the Apache section,
  slf4j-api1.7.36 in its MIT section, and zstd-jni1.5.7-17 in its BSD2-clause
  section. The separate retained SLF4J and Zstd license files contain those
  respective notices. These are distribution statements, to compare against
  the embedded JAR texts rather than replace them.
- Kafka `NOTICE` (`kafka-6-2410.data`, SHA
  `685a40de2dc7aab6c5a67d16b1363a7dbe7301b40e7ad604e1495b0fde5a8b93`)
  identifies Apache Kafka/ASF2026 and also describes broad distribution
  dependencies such as Jersey/CDDL. That does not establish that Jersey belongs
  to this five-JAR client classpath. No additional library is admitted from a
  distribution notice alone.
- The Kafka JRE and compiler JDK retain identical base LICENSE, additional
  licensing clarification and assembly-exception bytes. The base LICENSE hash
  is `4b9abebc4338048a7c2dc184e9f800deb349366bdf28eb23c2677a77b4c87726`;
  the clarification hash is
  `a69bce275ba7a3570af6579cb0f55682cd75fedfcd49e0e8e9022270c447c916`;
  the assembly-exception hash is
  `75292f03bf23d3db7c985aecc191029b93883200721ed23ed34a2e601463df33`.
  These texts describe GPL2 and the Classpath/assembly exceptions. This records
  their identity; it does not provide a new legal interpretation or approve
  redistribution of modified/copied JDK source.
- The actual Kafka image release text identifies Eclipse Adoptium Temurin
  JRE25.0.4.1+1, musl/aarch64, source repository
  `https://github.com/adoptium/jdk25u.git`, source revision `520406d87195`, and
  temurin-build revision `e6ba7dec3d07654074559310376a3ae89da5f4ac`.
  Its release-file hash is
  `68501bd21039d015b44daedf18854126d7237042603957e933ec40aab6061aab`.
  The actual compiler release identifies Temurin JDK25.0.5+8, glibc/aarch64,
  the same source repository, source revision `7ec19fb1eda7` and build revision
  `1cf43d7a3e77886bfea7d550a902e151a87d724d`. Its release-file hash is
  `08286c7d3e96769e411e4b56233478ce86f01f0e96803fb6af8f307e2b2527cb`.
  Those are retained artifact statements; this step has not fetched or rebuilt
  the named source revisions. Matching Java major versions supports the planned
  `--release 17` compiler/runtime split, with native compatibility still unproven.

The root's legal-alias supplement is separately pinned as SHA
`df10c6a7bbd7ec88da09dc7d40baf95364ebc998cc193a7390f15716d7b7b1a6`.
Neither it nor the image notices proves final-release source-to-binary equality.
The prior RC4-promotion/provenance limitation still needs a decision.

## Bounded ZIP data inspection

The independent parser in `kafka-admission/jars.py` reads fixed ZIP headers rather
than constructing `ZipFile`, which could allocate central-directory metadata
before admission. Its classic single-disk profile follows
[PKWARE APPNOTE6.3.10](https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT).
It validates EOCD extent, then checks central/local header lengths and fields,
data descriptors, paths, duplicate names, physical overlap and unindexed gaps. Metadata lengths
are admitted before variable slices. ZIP64, encryption, alternate Unicode-path
metadata, special members, unsupported flags/methods and unparsed central bytes
refuse. Other bounded extra fields remain inert hashes; they never change layout.

Each JAR is capped32MiB; central metadata2MiB/JAR; metadata8MiB across five JARs;
members20000/JAR and100000 total. Summed declared uncompressed sizes are capped
256MiB, without decompressing class/native members. Selected text is capped512KiB
per member and8MiB total, with a16MiB report. Selection covers manifests,
licenses/notices/dependencies, Maven POM/properties, service descriptors, signature
manifest text (.SF) and version.properties. Maven XML remains raw text; it is not parsed, resolved or
executed. Nothing invokes Java service discovery or loads a codec/native library.

Only selected text members are decompressed. Stored and raw DEFLATE are the only
methods admitted. [Python3.13 zlib](https://docs.python.org/3.13/library/zlib.html)
provides bounded `decompress(..., max_length)`; the script loops over at most64KiB
outputs, checks unconsumed/trailing bytes, EOF, exact extent and CRC32. It never
uses unbounded decompress/flush. CRC32 detects corruption; the immutable whole
JAR SHA-256 anchors input identity. No signature-verification claim is made.

Selected bytes are saved as flat generated `.text` filenames with their original
member name, extent, SHA and CRC evidence in `report.json`. A failure keeps a
scoped incomplete report and static failure code; it never admits execution.
The parser's10 source fixture methods cover stored/DEFLATE/descriptor originals,
expansion bombs, CRC corruption, encryption/method/ZIP64/multidisk/metadata caps,
paths/local mismatch, extras, selected/aggregate caps and truncation. They are
hand-authored fixtures and passed in root's isolated unit-second stage.

## Reviewed launcher and retained execution evidence

The new `kafka-artifact-launch.py` beside this note owns these stages and leaves the qualified
acquisition and legal launchers unchanged. It imports their exact hash-frozen
command, identity and regular-file copy functions. First copy frozen `jars.py` and
`jars_test.py` with their real names into a stopped admitted Python container;
run `python3 -I -B /work/jars_test.py -v`. After a clean matching receipt, copy
`jars.py`, hash-frozen `legal.py`, the original fifth inventory, every retained
`.data` payload and the exact legal supplement into another stopped container.
Freeze all source/input hashes before start; preserve copied readonly ownership.
Use network=none, memory=swap1GiB, CPU1/PID128, cap-dropALL/no-new-privileges,
no mounts, no ports, no host credentials and a hard external60s watchdog each.

The container data command is `python3 -I -B /work/jars.py --retained /work/retained
--supplement /work/legal-supplement.json --output /tmp/artifact-review`.
It verifies original inventory, every export, exact legal supplement and all five
final-path JAR identities before inspecting members. No network or compilation
is part of either stage. Preserve created/prestop/stopped/terminal state, logs,
exit/noOOM/resources and exact owned cleanup through the existing watchdog owner.

Copy outputs only from the stopped container. Admit a bounded flat archive with
at most100001 members, no extension headers/links/ancestors, exact generated
text/report basenames, selected-text sum8MiB, report16MiB, archive32MiB and a
separate finite copy timeout. Keep failed reports and original input identities.
The input snapshot is under49MiB; outputs under24MiB; an optional bounded output
archive adds at most32MiB. Count these copies against the existing128MiB research
reserve and1500MiB disk envelope, and check fresh disk before GO. No filesystem
quota or sufficiency claim is made. Do not keep parallel duplicate snapshots
once their exact provenance and root-authorized removal have been reviewed.

After reviewing and freezing the launcher itself, the root agent can run these
two host commands serially from the repository. The data command refuses a unit
receipt unless its source and owner hashes match, its started stage exited zero
without OOM or primary/cleanup faults, and exact owned retirement was confirmed.
Root ran unit-second and data-first successfully; exact receipt/report hashes
and the remaining no-execution boundary are in `kafka-artifact-verdict.md`.

```sh
python3 .tmp/implementation/kafka-artifact-launch.py unit first
python3 .tmp/implementation/kafka-artifact-launch.py data first .tmp/implementation/opfs-kafka-artifact-unit-first/terminal.json
```

Each attempt retains its source/input identities and bounded console log. A
hard watchdog stops the Docker CLI at60s; the outer owner then inspects and kills
only its exact labelled container if still running. It retains stopped state
before output copying and removal, confirms removal, and writes a terminal
receipt even after failure. Malformed create output is recovered using the exact
attempt name and label. The log sink stays open through the borrowed command's
failure cleanup so a secondary closed-stream error cannot hide the first fault.
The output parser checks physical tar headers before payload allocation and
rejects extension headers, links, duplicate/path tricks, unattributed text,
hash/size mismatches and nonzero appended data. It never extracts arbitrary tar
paths. An incomplete data report remains incomplete and makes the stage fail.

Parent must inspect the actual report, selected text, embedded versions/source
coordinates, any signature/service declarations and all retained image legal
references before choosing the precise test-only classpath. Codec JARs bundle
native binaries; they remain inert during this step. Runtime production SDK
approval is a separate decision. No compiler or broker GO follows automatically.

Source freeze: `jars.py`14544B SHA
`c3343d0f915eb11dcdbe5058a7876ff49a9395c4a91fc1b32aa2d1f941cce4bb`;
`jars_test.py`5251B SHA
`5b488544cdc249847d6fcb763a5d4a5af59af2ddb01f8ac9754f141ec370eb64`.
First-reader review keeps image distribution notices, the five-JAR client closure,
logical legal references and executable admission as distinct evidence. Embedded
